  "lineage": "Popular song-dance of young Yolngu men at Yirrkala in north-east Arnhem Land, sung for entertainment rather than ceremony, with light-hearted texts on everyday subjects set to the didjeridu and clapstick accompaniment of public song. Richard Waterman recorded djatpangarri at Yirrkala in the early 1950s, and recordings are held in the community archive of the Mulka Project.",
